<div id="p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:173%;">Appendix</span></p>
</div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Notation and Symbols for the Proof</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This subsection provides a comprehensive list of notations and symbols specific to the theoretical proof. The definitions align with the conventions in stochastic calculus and diffusion model analysis.
We build on the notations of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Common Terms</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> : Approximate ODE trajectory using the learned score <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},t)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> : True data distribution at noise level <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> : Distribution generated by simulating <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> : Norm upper bound for trajectories, satisfying <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall t,\left\|\mathbf{x}_{t}\right\|&lt;B/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall t,\left\|\mathbf{x}_{t}\right\|&lt;B/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}\sim p_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}\sim p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> : <math id="A1.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is sampled from distribution <math id="A1.I1.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>AdaSDE Terms</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A1.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math> : ODE discretization step size.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> : Hyperparameter controlling the noise injection ratio in the AdaSDE process.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t+\Delta t}^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t+\Delta t}^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> : AdaSDE forward process: <math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t+\Delta t}+\varepsilon_{t+\Delta t\rightarrow t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t+\Delta t}+\varepsilon_{t+\Delta t\rightarrow t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>: Gaussian noise <math id="A1.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I2.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> : AdaSDE backward process: <math id="A1.I2.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t+\Delta t}^{\gamma},t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t\rightarrow t\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t+\Delta t}^{\gamma},t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t\rightarrow t\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I2.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{AdaSDE}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝖲𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{AdaSDE}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> : Applies the AdaSDE operation with parameter <math id="A1.I2.i6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> to state <math id="A1.I2.i6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I2.i7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>: The solution to
<math id="A1.I2.i7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}=-ts_{\theta}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t+\Delta t},t+\Delta t\right)dt," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}=-ts_{\theta}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t+\Delta t},t+\Delta t\right)dt,</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Lipschitz and Error Bounds</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A1.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> : Temporal Lipschitz constant:<math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|ts_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},t)-ts_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},s)\right\|\leq L_{0}|t-s|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|ts_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},t)-ts_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},s)\right\|\leq L_{0}|t-s|</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> : Boundedness of the learned score: <math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|ts_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},t)\right\|\leq L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|ts_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},t)\right\|\leq L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> : Spatial Lipschitz constant:<math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|ts_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},t)-ts_{\theta}(\mathbf{y},t)\right\|\leq L_{2}\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|ts_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},t)-ts_{\theta}(\mathbf{y},t)\right\|\leq L_{2}\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> : Score matching error:<math id="A1.I3.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|t\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\log p_{t}(\mathbf{x})-ts_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},t)\right\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|t\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\log p_{t}(\mathbf{x})-ts_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},t)\right\|</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Special Operators</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A1.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{ODE}\left(\mathbf{x},t_{1}\rightarrow t_{2}\right):" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.278em">)</mo></mrow><mo>:</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{ODE}\left(\mathbf{x},t_{1}\rightarrow t_{2}\right):</annotation></semantics></math> Ground Truth backward ODE evolution under the exact score from <math id="A1.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.I4.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}\left(\mathbf{x},t_{1}\rightarrow t_{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}\left(\mathbf{x},t_{1}\rightarrow t_{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> : Approximate ODE evolution using the learned score <math id="A1.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="*" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">*</annotation></semantics></math>: Convolution operator between distributions, e.g., <math id="A1.I4.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P*R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P*R</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the convolution of <math id="A1.I4.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I4.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I4.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> : Time-reversal marker, e.g., <math id="A1.I4.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\leftarrow}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\leftarrow}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Key Process Terms</h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A1.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}^{\mathbf{x},\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}^{\mathbf{x},\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> : Distribution at noise level <math id="A1.I5.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> after applying the AdaSDE process starting from state <math id="A1.I5.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}_{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝖲𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}_{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> : Distribution generated by the AdaSDE algorithm.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I5.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{x},\xi_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{x},\xi_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> : i.i.d Gaussian noise: <math id="A1.I5.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{x}\sim\mathcal{N}\left(0,\sigma^{2}I_{d}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{x}\sim\mathcal{N}\left(0,\sigma^{2}I_{d}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I5.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{y}\sim\mathcal{N}\left(0,\sigma^{2}I_{d}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{y}\sim\mathcal{N}\left(0,\sigma^{2}I_{d}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6 </span>Error Dynamics</h3>

<div id="A1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A1.I6" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I6.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e(t):=\left\|\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\leftarrow}-\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{\leftarrow}\right\|:" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e(t):=\left\|\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\leftarrow}-\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{\leftarrow}\right\|:</annotation></semantics></math> Error dynamics in the time-reversed coordinate system in <math id="A1.I6.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I6.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> : Noise merging probability:<math id="A1.I6.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2Q\left(\frac{B}{2\sqrt{(t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t)^{2}-t^{2}}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2Q\left(\frac{B}{2\sqrt{(t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t)^{2}-t^{2}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.I6.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(r)=\operatorname{Pr}(a\geq r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(r)=\operatorname{Pr}(a\geq r)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.I6.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I6.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I6.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I6.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I6.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}(\cdot,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}(\cdot,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> : Wasserstein-1 distance.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I6.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I6.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I6.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I6.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A1.I6.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\cdot,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\cdot,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> : Total Variation (TV) distance.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Where <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{t+\Delta t\rightarrow t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\sim\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbf{0},\left((t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t)^{2}-(t+\Delta t)^{2}\right)\bm{I}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{t+\Delta t\rightarrow t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\sim\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbf{0},\left((t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t)^{2}-(t+\Delta t)^{2}\right)\bm{I}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. For the sake of simplifying symbolic representation and facilitating comprehension, in the following proof, we use <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{AdaSDE}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝖲𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{AdaSDE}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> to denote <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> in the above processes. In various theorems, we will refer to a function <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(r):\mathbb{R}^{+}\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(r):\mathbb{R}^{+}\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1/2)</annotation></semantics></math>, defined as the Gaussian tail probability <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(r)=\operatorname{Pr}(a\geq r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(r)=\operatorname{Pr}(a\geq r)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proofs of Main Theoretical Results</h2>

<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Upper Bound on ODE Discretization Error)<span id="Thmlemma1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">[</span><a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">]</span></cite><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
Let <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}=\mathsf{ODE}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t+\Delta t},t+\Delta t\rightarrow t\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}=\mathsf{ODE}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t+\Delta t},t+\Delta t\rightarrow t\right)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the solution of the backward ODE under the exact score field,
and <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}=\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}\left(\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t+\Delta t},t+\Delta t\rightarrow t\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}=\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}\left(\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t+\Delta t},t+\Delta t\rightarrow t\right)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the discretized ODE solution using the learned field <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assume <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies:
<br class="ltx_break">1. Temporal Lipschitz Continuity:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|ts_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},t)-ts_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},s)\right\|\leq L_{0}|t-s|\quad\forall\mathbf{x},t,s" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|ts_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},t)-ts_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},s)\right\|\leq L_{0}|t-s|\quad\forall\mathbf{x},t,s</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">2. Boundedness:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|ts_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},t)\right\|\leq L_{1}\quad\forall\mathbf{x},t" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|ts_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},t)\right\|\leq L_{1}\quad\forall\mathbf{x},t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">3. Spatial Lipschitz Continuity:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|ts_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},t)-ts_{\theta}(\mathbf{y},t)\right\|\leq L_{2}\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|\quad\forall\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y},t" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|ts_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},t)-ts_{\theta}(\mathbf{y},t)\right\|\leq L_{2}\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|\quad\forall\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y},t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then the discretization error satisfies:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\mathbf{x}_{t}-\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}\right\|\leq e^{L_{2}\Delta t}\left(\left\|\mathbf{x}_{t+\Delta t}-\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t+\Delta t}\right\|+\left(\Delta t\left(L_{2}L_{1}+L_{0}\right)+\epsilon_{t}\right)\Delta t\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\mathbf{x}_{t}-\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}\right\|\leq e^{L_{2}\Delta t}\left(\left\|\mathbf{x}_{t+\Delta t}-\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t+\Delta t}\right\|+\left(\Delta t\left(L_{2}L_{1}+L_{0}\right)+\epsilon_{t}\right)\Delta t\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Step 1: Definition of Time-Reversed Processes
<br class="ltx_break">Introduce time-reversed variables <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\leftarrow}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\leftarrow}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{\leftarrow}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{\leftarrow}</annotation></semantics></math> governed by:
where <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is the integer satisfying <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="t\in[t^{\prime},t^{\prime}+\Delta t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[t^{\prime},t^{\prime}+\Delta t)</annotation></semantics></math>, corresponding to discrete timesteps.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Step 2: Error Dynamics
<br class="ltx_break">Define the error <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e(t):=\left\|\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\leftarrow}-\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{\leftarrow}\right\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e(t):=\left\|\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\leftarrow}-\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{\leftarrow}\right\|</annotation></semantics></math>. Its derivative satisfies:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{d}{dt}e(t)\leq\left\|t\nabla\log p_{t}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\leftarrow}\right)-ts_{\theta}\left(\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t^{\prime}+\Delta t}^{\leftarrow},t^{\prime}+\Delta t\right)\right\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dt}e(t)\leq\left\|t\nabla\log p_{t}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\leftarrow}\right)-ts_{\theta}\left(\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t^{\prime}+\Delta t}^{\leftarrow},t^{\prime}+\Delta t\right)\right\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Decompose the right-hand side:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex17X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\underbrace{\left\|t\nabla\log p_{t}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\leftarrow}\right)-ts_{\theta}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\leftarrow},t\right)\right\|}_{\text{Approximation Error }\epsilon_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msup><mo>)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>Approximation Error </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\underbrace{\left\|t\nabla\log p_{t}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\leftarrow}\right)-ts_{\theta}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\leftarrow},t\right)\right\|}_{\text{Approximation Error }\epsilon_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex17Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\underbrace{\left\|ts_{\theta}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\leftarrow},t\right)-ts_{\theta}\left(\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{\leftarrow},t\right)\right\|}_{L_{2}\left\|\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\leftarrow}-\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{\leftarrow}\right\|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\underbrace{\left\|ts_{\theta}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\leftarrow},t\right)-ts_{\theta}\left(\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{\leftarrow},t\right)\right\|}_{L_{2}\left\|\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\leftarrow}-\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{\leftarrow}\right\|}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex17Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\underbrace{\left\|ts_{\theta}\left(\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{\leftarrow},t\right)-ts_{\theta}\left(\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t^{\prime}+\Delta t}^{\leftarrow},t\textquoteright+\Delta t\right)\right\|}_{\text{Temporal Discretization Error }}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>’</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Temporal Discretization Error </mtext></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\underbrace{\left\|ts_{\theta}\left(\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{\leftarrow},t\right)-ts_{\theta}\left(\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t^{\prime}+\Delta t}^{\leftarrow},t\textquoteright+\Delta t\right)\right\|}_{\text{Temporal Discretization Error }}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Step 3: Temporal Discretization Error Bound
<br class="ltx_break">Further decompose the temporal discretization error:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex18X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex18X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left\|ts_{\theta}\left(\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{\leftarrow},t\right)-ts_{\theta}\left(\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t^{\prime}+\Delta t}^{\leftarrow},t\right)\right\|+\left\|ts_{\theta}\left(\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t^{\prime}+\Delta t}^{\leftarrow},t\right)-ts_{\theta}\left(\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t^{\prime}+\Delta t}^{\leftarrow},t^{\prime}+\Delta t\right)\right\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left\|ts_{\theta}\left(\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{\leftarrow},t\right)-ts_{\theta}\left(\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t^{\prime}+\Delta t}^{\leftarrow},t\right)\right\|+\left\|ts_{\theta}\left(\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t^{\prime}+\Delta t}^{\leftarrow},t\right)-ts_{\theta}\left(\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t^{\prime}+\Delta t}^{\leftarrow},t^{\prime}+\Delta t\right)\right\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex18Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex18Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq L_{0}|t^{\prime}+\Delta t-t^{\prime}|+L_{2}\|\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{\leftarrow}-\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t^{\prime}+\Delta_{t}}^{\leftarrow}\|\quad\text{ (Lipschitz continuity) }" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext> (Lipschitz continuity)</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq L_{0}|t^{\prime}+\Delta t-t^{\prime}|+L_{2}\|\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{\leftarrow}-\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t^{\prime}+\Delta_{t}}^{\leftarrow}\|\quad\text{ (Lipschitz continuity) }</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex18Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex18Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq L_{0}\Delta t+L_{2}\left(\left\|\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{\leftarrow}-\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t^{\prime}+\Delta t}^{\leftarrow}\right\|\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq L_{0}\Delta t+L_{2}\left(\left\|\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{\leftarrow}-\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t^{\prime}+\Delta t}^{\leftarrow}\right\|\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using the boundedness condition <math id="A2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|d\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{\leftarrow}/dt\right\|\leq L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|d\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{\leftarrow}/dt\right\|\leq L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{\leftarrow}-\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t^{\prime}+\Delta t}^{\leftarrow}\right\|\leq\int_{t}^{t^{\prime}+\Delta t}\left\|d\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{s}^{\leftarrow}\right\|ds\leq L_{1}\Delta t" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mi>t</mi><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{\leftarrow}-\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t^{\prime}+\Delta t}^{\leftarrow}\right\|\leq\int_{t}^{t^{\prime}+\Delta t}\left\|d\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{s}^{\leftarrow}\right\|ds\leq L_{1}\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Step 4: Composite Differential Inequality
<br class="ltx_break">Combining all terms, the error dynamics satisfy:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{dt}e(t)\leq L_{2}e(t)+\left(\epsilon_{t}+L_{0}\Delta t+L_{2}L_{1}\Delta t\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dt}e(t)\leq L_{2}e(t)+\left(\epsilon_{t}+L_{0}\Delta t+L_{2}L_{1}\Delta t\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Step 5: Gronwall’s Inequality Application
<br class="ltx_break">Integrate over <math id="A2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\left[t,t+\Delta t\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\left[t,t+\Delta t\right]</annotation></semantics></math> and apply Gronwall’s inequality:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\left(t\right)\leq e^{L_{2}\Delta t}\left(e\left(t+\Delta t\right)+\left(\epsilon_{t}+\Delta t\left(L_{0}+L_{2}L_{1}\right)\right)\Delta t\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\left(t\right)\leq e^{L_{2}\Delta t}\left(e\left(t+\Delta t\right)+\left(\epsilon_{t}+\Delta t\left(L_{0}+L_{2}L_{1}\right)\right)\Delta t\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(TV Distance Between Gaussian Perturbations)<span id="Thmlemma2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{x}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2}I_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{x}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2}I_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{y}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2}I_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{y}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2}I_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> be independent noise vectors. For <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}^{\prime}=\mathbf{x}+\xi_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}^{\prime}=\mathbf{x}+\xi_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}^{\prime}=\mathbf{y}+\xi_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}^{\prime}=\mathbf{y}+\xi_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, their total variation distance satisfies:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime},\mathbf{y}^{\prime})=1-2Q\left(\frac{\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|}{2\sigma}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime},\mathbf{y}^{\prime})=1-2Q\left(\frac{\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|}{2\sigma}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(r)=\Pr_{a\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)}(a\geq r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(r)=\Pr_{a\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)}(a\geq r)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}</annotation></semantics></math>. The TV distance is:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{TV}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime},\mathbf{y}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{TV}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime},\mathbf{y}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}|\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{z};\mathbf{x},\sigma^{2}I_{d})-\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{z};\mathbf{y},\sigma^{2}I_{d})|dz" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}|\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{z};\mathbf{x},\sigma^{2}I_{d})-\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{z};\mathbf{y},\sigma^{2}I_{d})|dz</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\left|\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{z}-\delta;\mathbf{0},\sigma^{2}I_{d})-\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{z};\mathbf{0},\sigma^{2}I_{d})\right|dz" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\left|\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{z}-\delta;\mathbf{0},\sigma^{2}I_{d})-\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{z};\mathbf{0},\sigma^{2}I_{d})\right|dz</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Through orthogonal transformation <math id="A2.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> aligning <math id="A2.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> with the first axis:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\delta=(\|\delta\|,0,...,0)^{\top}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\delta=(\|\delta\|,0,...,0)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p16.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p16.2.1" class="ltx_text">By rotational invariance of Gaussians:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime},\mathbf{y}^{\prime})=\mathsf{TV}\left(\mathcal{N}(\|\delta\|,\sigma^{2}),\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2})\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime},\mathbf{y}^{\prime})=\mathsf{TV}\left(\mathcal{N}(\|\delta\|,\sigma^{2}),\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">For 1D Gaussians <math id="A2.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(\mu,\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(\mu,\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{TV}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{TV}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\left|\phi\left(\frac{\mathbf{z}-\mu}{\sigma}\right)-\phi\left(\frac{\mathbf{z}}{\sigma}\right)\right|dz" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mi>σ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>σ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\left|\phi\left(\frac{\mathbf{z}-\mu}{\sigma}\right)-\phi\left(\frac{\mathbf{z}}{\sigma}\right)\right|dz</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\Phi\left(-\frac{\mu}{2\sigma}\right)-\Phi\left(\frac{\mu}{2\sigma}\right)\quad\text{(By symmetry)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mtext>(By symmetry)</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Phi\left(-\frac{\mu}{2\sigma}\right)-\Phi\left(\frac{\mu}{2\sigma}\right)\quad\text{(By symmetry)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1-2\Phi\left(\frac{\mu}{2\sigma}\right)=2Q\left(\frac{\mu}{2\sigma}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-2\Phi\left(\frac{\mu}{2\sigma}\right)=2Q\left(\frac{\mu}{2\sigma}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p17.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p17.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|</annotation></semantics></math>.
then:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime},\mathbf{y}^{\prime})=1-2Q\left(\frac{\|\delta\|}{2\sigma}\right)=1-2Q\left(\frac{\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|}{2\sigma}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime},\mathbf{y}^{\prime})=1-2Q\left(\frac{\|\delta\|}{2\sigma}\right)=1-2Q\left(\frac{\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|}{2\sigma}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p17.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p17.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}^{\mathbf{x},\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}^{\mathbf{x},\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}^{\mathbf{y},\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}^{\mathbf{y},\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the densities of <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}_{t}^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}_{t}^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively. After applying AdaSDE with noise injection from <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math> followed by backward ODE evolution, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}\left(p_{t}^{\mathbf{x},\gamma},p_{t}^{\mathbf{y},\gamma}\right)\leq(1-\lambda(\gamma))\mathsf{TV}\left(p_{t}^{\mathbf{x}},p_{t}^{\mathbf{y}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>𝐲</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}\left(p_{t}^{\mathbf{x},\gamma},p_{t}^{\mathbf{y},\gamma}\right)\leq(1-\lambda(\gamma))\mathsf{TV}\left(p_{t}^{\mathbf{x}},p_{t}^{\mathbf{y}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(\gamma)=2Q\left(\dfrac{B}{2\sqrt{(t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t)^{2}-t^{2}}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(\gamma)=2Q\left(\dfrac{B}{2\sqrt{(t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t)^{2}-t^{2}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider states <math id="A2.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> at noise level <math id="A2.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{x}_{t}-\mathbf{y}_{t}\|\leq B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{x}_{t}-\mathbf{y}_{t}\|\leq B</annotation></semantics></math>. The AdaSDE process first perturbs both states to noise level <math id="A2.p18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math> through Gaussian noise injection:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{x}_{t}+\xi_{x},\ \xi_{x}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,[(t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t)^{2}-t^{2}]I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{x}_{t}+\xi_{x},\ \xi_{x}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,[(t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t)^{2}-t^{2}]I)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{y}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{y}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{y}_{t}+\xi_{y},\ \xi_{y}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,[(t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t)^{2}-t^{2}]I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{y}_{t}+\xi_{y},\ \xi_{y}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,[(t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t)^{2}-t^{2}]I)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">We construct a coupling between the noise injections: when <math id="A2.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}=\mathbf{y}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}=\mathbf{y}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, set <math id="A2.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{x}=\xi_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{x}=\xi_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>; otherwise use reflection coupling. By Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 (TV Distance Between Gaussian Perturbations). ‣ Appendix B Proofs of Main Theoretical Results ‣ Adaptive Stochastic Coefficients for Accelerating Diffusion Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, the merging probability satisfies:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda(\gamma)=2Q\left(\frac{\|\mathbf{x}_{t}-\mathbf{y}_{t}\|}{2\sigma_{t}(\gamma)}\right)\geq 2Q\left(\frac{B}{2\sigma_{t}(\gamma)}\right)\quad(\text{since }\|\mathbf{x}_{t}-\mathbf{y}_{t}\|\leq B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>since </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda(\gamma)=2Q\left(\frac{\|\mathbf{x}_{t}-\mathbf{y}_{t}\|}{2\sigma_{t}(\gamma)}\right)\geq 2Q\left(\frac{B}{2\sigma_{t}(\gamma)}\right)\quad(\text{since }\|\mathbf{x}_{t}-\mathbf{y}_{t}\|\leq B)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p19.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p19.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(r)=\Pr_{a\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)}(a\geq r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(r)=\Pr_{a\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)}(a\geq r)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">This implies:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\mathbf{x}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\neq\mathbf{y}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\mid\mathbf{x}_{t}\neq\mathbf{y}_{t})\leq 1-\lambda(\gamma)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\mathbf{x}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\neq\mathbf{y}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\mid\mathbf{x}_{t}\neq\mathbf{y}_{t})\leq 1-\lambda(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p20.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p20.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> quantifies the minimum merging probability between the Gaussian perturbations.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">The subsequent backward ODE evolution preserves this coupling relationship because both trajectories are driven by the same learned score <math id="A2.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\gamma}\neq\mathbf{y}_{t}^{\gamma})\leq(1-\lambda(\gamma))\mathbb{P}(\mathbf{x}_{t}\neq\mathbf{y}_{t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\gamma}\neq\mathbf{y}_{t}^{\gamma})\leq(1-\lambda(\gamma))\mathbb{P}(\mathbf{x}_{t}\neq\mathbf{y}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">Through the coupling characterization of total variation distance, we conclude:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(p_{t}^{\mathbf{x},\gamma},p_{t}^{\mathbf{y},\gamma})\leq(1-\lambda(\gamma))\mathsf{TV}(p_{t}^{\mathbf{x}},p_{t}^{\mathbf{y}})\qed" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>𝐲</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(p_{t}^{\mathbf{x},\gamma},p_{t}^{\mathbf{y},\gamma})\leq(1-\lambda(\gamma))\mathsf{TV}(p_{t}^{\mathbf{x}},p_{t}^{\mathbf{y}})\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4</span></span><span id="Thmlemma4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(AdaSDE Error Propagation)<span id="Thmlemma4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t+\Delta t}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t+\Delta t}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be an initial point. Define exact and approximate ODE solutions:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex38X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex38X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex38X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathsf{ODE}\bigl(\mathbf{x}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t},\,t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t\!\to t\bigr)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathsf{ODE}\bigl(\mathbf{x}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t},\,t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t\!\to t\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex38Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex38Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex38Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}\bigl(\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t},\,t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t\!\to t\bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}\bigl(\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t},\,t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t\!\to t\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under AdaSDE with noise injection <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+\Delta t\to t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+\Delta t\to t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{x}_{t}-\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}\|\leq B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{x}_{t}-\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}\|\leq B</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a coupling such that:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bigl\|\,\mathbf{x}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}-\,\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\bigr\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.392em">−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bigl\|\,\mathbf{x}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}-\,\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\bigr\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex39.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq e^{L_{2}(1+\gamma)\Delta t}(1+\gamma)\left[\Delta t(L_{2}L_{1}+L_{0})+\epsilon_{t}\right]\Delta t," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq e^{L_{2}(1+\gamma)\Delta t}(1+\gamma)\left[\Delta t(L_{2}L_{1}+L_{0})+\epsilon_{t}\right]\Delta t,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{0},L_{1},L_{2},\epsilon_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{0},L_{1},L_{2},\epsilon_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> are the Lipschitz/boundedness/approximation constants for <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and discretization errors.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">B<span id="A2.p23.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">y Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem1a" title="Theorem 1. ‣ B.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs of Main Theoretical Results ‣ Adaptive Stochastic Coefficients for Accelerating Diffusion Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> (ODE Discretization Error), the local truncation error satisfies:</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathbf{x}_{t}-\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathbf{x}_{t}-\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex40.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq e^{L_{2}(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\Big[\|\mathbf{x}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}-\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq e^{L_{2}(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\Big[\|\mathbf{x}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}-\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\underbrace{\big((1+\gamma)\Delta t(L_{2}L_{1}+L_{0})+\epsilon_{t}\big)(1+\gamma)\Delta t}_{\text{Local discretization error}}\Big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Local discretization error</mtext></munder><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\underbrace{\big((1+\gamma)\Delta t(L_{2}L_{1}+L_{0})+\epsilon_{t}\big)(1+\gamma)\Delta t}_{\text{Local discretization error}}\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p24" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p24.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p24.1.1" class="ltx_text">Applying AdaSDE’s noise injection with variance <math id="A2.p24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}=(t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t)^{2}-t^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}=(t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t)^{2}-t^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 (TV Distance Between Gaussian Perturbations). ‣ Appendix B Proofs of Main Theoretical Results ‣ Adaptive Stochastic Coefficients for Accelerating Diffusion Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> gives:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\|\mathbf{x}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}-\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\|\mathbf{x}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}-\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex42.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(1-\lambda(\gamma))\|\mathbf{x}_{t}-\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}\|," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(1-\lambda(\gamma))\|\mathbf{x}_{t}-\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}\|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p24.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p24.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the merging probability <math id="A2.p24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(\gamma)=2\,Q\bigl(\dfrac{B}{2\,\sqrt{(t+(1+\gamma)\,\Delta t)^{2}-t^{2}}}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(\gamma)=2\,Q\bigl(\dfrac{B}{2\,\sqrt{(t+(1+\gamma)\,\Delta t)^{2}-t^{2}}}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math> dominates the coupling effectiveness.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p25" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p25.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p25.1.1" class="ltx_text">Multiplying by <math id="A2.p25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\lambda(\gamma))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\lambda(\gamma))</annotation></semantics></math> from partial revert and adding the local ODE approximation error leads to the stated bound:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bigl\|\,\mathbf{x}_{t+(1+\gamma\Delta t)}-\,\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t+(1+\gamma\Delta t)}\bigr\|\;\;\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.392em">−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.560em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bigl\|\,\mathbf{x}_{t+(1+\gamma\Delta t)}-\,\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t+(1+\gamma\Delta t)}\bigr\|\;\;\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;\;\bigl(1-\lambda(\gamma)\bigr)\,\bigl\|\,\mathbf{x}_{t}-\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}\bigr\|\;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;\;\bigl(1-\lambda(\gamma)\bigr)\,\bigl\|\,\mathbf{x}_{t}-\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}\bigr\|\;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\;e^{L_{2}\,(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\,(1+\gamma)\bigl[(1+\gamma)\Delta t(\,L_{2}L_{1}+L_{0})\;+\;\epsilon_{t}\bigr]\,\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\;e^{L_{2}\,(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\,(1+\gamma)\bigl[(1+\gamma)\Delta t(\,L_{2}L_{1}+L_{0})\;+\;\epsilon_{t}\bigr]\,\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=e^{L_{2}\,(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\,(1+\gamma)\bigl[\Delta t(\,L_{2}L_{1}+L_{0})\;+\;\epsilon_{t}\bigr]\,\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=e^{L_{2}\,(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\,(1+\gamma)\bigl[\Delta t(\,L_{2}L_{1}+L_{0})\;+\;\epsilon_{t}\bigr]\,\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p26" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p26.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p26.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5</span></span><span id="Thmlemma5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Connection of Wasserstein-1 distance and Norm)<span id="Thmlemma5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> be two probability distributions over a space <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma(p_{1},p_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma(p_{1},p_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the set of all joint distributions with marginals <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. The Wasserstein-1 distance between <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}(p_{1},p_{2})=\inf_{\psi\in\Gamma(p_{1},p_{2})}\mathbb{E}_{(\mathbf{x}_{1},\mathbf{x}_{2})\sim\psi}\left[\|\mathbf{x}_{1}-\mathbf{x}_{2}\|\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}(p_{1},p_{2})=\inf_{\psi\in\Gamma(p_{1},p_{2})}\mathbb{E}_{(\mathbf{x}_{1},\mathbf{x}_{2})\sim\psi}\left[\|\mathbf{x}_{1}-\mathbf{x}_{2}\|\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmlemma5.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the L1 norm. Furthermore, for independent samples <math id="Thmlemma5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{1}\sim p_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{1}\sim p_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{2}\sim p_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{2}\sim p_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}(p_{1},p_{2})\leq\mathbb{E}\left[\|\mathbf{x}_{1}-\mathbf{x}_{2}\|\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}(p_{1},p_{2})\leq\mathbb{E}\left[\|\mathbf{x}_{1}-\mathbf{x}_{2}\|\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma5.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with equality if and only if the coupling <math id="Thmlemma5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> is optimal.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6</span></span><span id="Thmlemma6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(P*R,Q*R)\leq\mathsf{TV}(P,Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(P*R,Q*R)\leq\mathsf{TV}(P,Q)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Thmlemma6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for independent distributions <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P,Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P,Q</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>.The inequality <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(P*R,Q*R)=\mathsf{TV}(P,Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(P*R,Q*R)=\mathsf{TV}(P,Q)</annotation></semantics></math> holds if and only if <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is a degenerate distribution.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p27" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p27.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p27.1.1" class="ltx_text">1. Total Variation Distance Definition</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p28" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p28.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p28.1.1" class="ltx_text">The total variation distance between two distributions <math id="A2.p28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(P,Q)=\frac{1}{2}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}|p(\mathbf{x})-q(\mathbf{x})|d\mathbf{x}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(P,Q)=\frac{1}{2}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}|p(\mathbf{x})-q(\mathbf{x})|d\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p28.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p28.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.p28.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p28.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> are the probability density functions of <math id="A2.p28.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p28.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p29" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p29.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p29.1.1" class="ltx_text">2. Convolution Definition</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p30" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p30.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p30.1.1" class="ltx_text">The convolution of two distributions <math id="A2.p30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P*R)(\mathbf{x})=\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}p(\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y})r(\mathbf{y})d\mathbf{y}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P*R)(\mathbf{x})=\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}p(\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y})r(\mathbf{y})d\mathbf{y}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p31" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p31.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p31.1.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, for <math id="A2.p31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> :</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Q*R)(\mathbf{x})=\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}q(\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y})r(\mathbf{y})d\mathbf{y}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Q*R)(\mathbf{x})=\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}q(\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y})r(\mathbf{y})d\mathbf{y}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p32" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p32.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p32.1.1" class="ltx_text">3. TV Distance for Convolved Distributions</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p33" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p33.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p33.1.1" class="ltx_text">We want to compute <math id="A2.p33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(P*R,Q*R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(P*R,Q*R)</annotation></semantics></math>, which is:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{TV}(P*R,Q*R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{TV}(P*R,Q*R)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex51.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\left|(P*R)(\mathbf{x})-(Q*R)(\mathbf{x})\right|dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\left|(P*R)(\mathbf{x})-(Q*R)(\mathbf{x})\right|dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\left|\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}(p(\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y})-q(\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}))r(\mathbf{y})dy\right|dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\left|\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}(p(\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y})-q(\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}))r(\mathbf{y})dy\right|dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p34" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p34.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p34.1.1" class="ltx_text">Applying triangle inequality, we obtain:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(P*R,Q*R)\leq\frac{1}{2}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\left(\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}|p(\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y})-q(\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y})|r(\mathbf{y})d\mathbf{y}\right)d\mathbf{x}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(P*R,Q*R)\leq\frac{1}{2}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\left(\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}|p(\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y})-q(\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y})|r(\mathbf{y})d\mathbf{y}\right)d\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p34.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p34.2.1" class="ltx_text">Using Fubini’s theorem, we can swap the order of integration:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(P*R,Q*R)\leq\frac{1}{2}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\left(\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}|p(\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y})-q(\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y})|d\mathbf{x}\right)r(\mathbf{y})d\mathbf{y}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(P*R,Q*R)\leq\frac{1}{2}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\left(\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}|p(\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y})-q(\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y})|d\mathbf{x}\right)r(\mathbf{y})d\mathbf{y}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p34.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p34.3.1" class="ltx_text">For fixed <math id="A2.p34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, the inner integral is:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}|p(\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y})-q(\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y})|d\mathbf{x}=\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}|p(\mathbf{x})-q(\mathbf{x})|d\mathbf{x}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" lspace="0.278em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.1389em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}|p(\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y})-q(\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y})|d\mathbf{x}=\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}|p(\mathbf{x})-q(\mathbf{x})|d\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p34.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p34.4.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, we obtain:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p35" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(P*R,Q*R)\leq\frac{1}{2}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\left(\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}|p(\mathbf{x})-q(\mathbf{x})|d\mathbf{x}\right)r(\mathbf{y})d\mathbf{y}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(P*R,Q*R)\leq\frac{1}{2}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\left(\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}|p(\mathbf{x})-q(\mathbf{x})|d\mathbf{x}\right)r(\mathbf{y})d\mathbf{y}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(P*R,Q*R)\leq\mathsf{TV}(P,Q)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(P*R,Q*R)\leq\mathsf{TV}(P,Q)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p35.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p35.1.1" class="ltx_text">The inequality <math id="A2.p35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(P*R,Q*R)=\mathsf{TV}(P,Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(P*R,Q*R)=\mathsf{TV}(P,Q)</annotation></semantics></math> holds if and only if <math id="A2.p35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is a degenerate distribution.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p36" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p36.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p36.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1a" title="Theorem 1. ‣ B.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs of Main Theoretical Results ‣ Adaptive Stochastic Coefficients for Accelerating Diffusion Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="Thmtheorem1a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math> be the initial noise level. Let <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}=\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t+\Delta t},t+\Delta t\rightarrow t\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}=\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t+\Delta t},t+\Delta t\rightarrow t\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the distribution induced by simulating the ODE with learned drift <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume:
<br class="ltx_break">1. The learned drift <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ts_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ts_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},t)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz in <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, bounded by <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz in <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">2. The approximation error <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left\|ts_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},t)-t\nabla\log p_{t}(\mathbf{x})\right\|\leq\epsilon_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|ts_{\theta}(\mathbf{x},t)-t\nabla\log p_{t}(\mathbf{x})\right\|\leq\epsilon_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">3. All trajectories are bounded by <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B/2</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">Then, the Wasserstein-1 distance between the generated distribution <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the true distribution <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by:
<br class="ltx_break"></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex58X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex58X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{1}\left(p_{t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},p_{t}\right)\leq B\cdot\mathsf{TV}\left(p_{t+\Delta t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},p_{t+\Delta t}\right)+e^{L_{2}\Delta t}\cdot\left(\Delta t\left(L_{2}L_{1}+L_{0}\right)+\epsilon_{t}\right)\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{1}\left(p_{t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},p_{t}\right)\leq B\cdot\mathsf{TV}\left(p_{t+\Delta t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},p_{t+\Delta t}\right)+e^{L_{2}\Delta t}\cdot\left(\Delta t\left(L_{2}L_{1}+L_{0}\right)+\epsilon_{t}\right)\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math> is the step size</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}=\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t+\Delta t},t+\Delta t\rightarrow t\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}=\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t+\Delta t},t+\Delta t\rightarrow t\right)</annotation></semantics></math> with the corresponding distribution <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}=\mathsf{ODE}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t+\Delta t},t+\Delta t\rightarrow t\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}=\mathsf{ODE}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t+\Delta t},t+\Delta t\rightarrow t\right)</annotation></semantics></math> (simulated under the true score).
The proof bounds <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}\left(p_{t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},p_{t}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}\left(p_{t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},p_{t}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> via triangular inequality:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}\left(p_{t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},p_{t}\right)\leq W_{1}\left(p_{t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},\hat{p}_{t}\right)+W_{1}\left(\hat{p}_{t},p_{t}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}\left(p_{t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},p_{t}\right)\leq W_{1}\left(p_{t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},\hat{p}_{t}\right)+W_{1}\left(\hat{p}_{t},p_{t}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then we can bound two terms seperately.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">1. gradient error: By bounded-diameter inequality,</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}\left(p_{t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},\hat{p}_{t}\right)\leq B\cdot\mathsf{TV}\left(p_{t+\Delta t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},p_{t+\Delta t}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}\left(p_{t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},\hat{p}_{t}\right)\leq B\cdot\mathsf{TV}\left(p_{t+\Delta t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},p_{t+\Delta t}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">2. discretization error: Using Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Upper Bound on ODE Discretization Error). ‣ Appendix B Proofs of Main Theoretical Results ‣ Adaptive Stochastic Coefficients for Accelerating Diffusion Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> (discretization bound), given <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}\sim p_{t},\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}\sim\hat{p}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}\sim p_{t},\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}\sim\hat{p}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}-\mathbf{x}_{t}\right\|\leq e^{L_{2}\Delta t}\cdot\left(\Delta t\left(L_{2}L_{1}+L_{0}\right)+\epsilon_{t}\right)\Delta t" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}-\mathbf{x}_{t}\right\|\leq e^{L_{2}\Delta t}\cdot\left(\Delta t\left(L_{2}L_{1}+L_{0}\right)+\epsilon_{t}\right)\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">where the exponential factor arises from Gronwall’s inequality applied to the Lipschitz drift. According to Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma5" title="Lemma 5 (Connection of Wasserstein-1 distance and Norm). ‣ Appendix B Proofs of Main Theoretical Results ‣ Adaptive Stochastic Coefficients for Accelerating Diffusion Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we can
combine terms via triangular inequality:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}\left(p_{t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},p_{t}\right)\leq\underbrace{B\cdot\mathsf{TV}\left(p_{t+\Delta t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},p_{t+\Delta t}\right)}_{\text{gradient error }}+\underbrace{e^{L_{2}\Delta t}\cdot\left(\Delta t\left(L_{2}L_{1}+L_{0}\right)+\epsilon_{t}\right)\Delta t}_{\text{discretization error }}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>gradient error </mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>discretization error </mtext></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}\left(p_{t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},p_{t}\right)\leq\underbrace{B\cdot\mathsf{TV}\left(p_{t+\Delta t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},p_{t+\Delta t}\right)}_{\text{gradient error }}+\underbrace{e^{L_{2}\Delta t}\cdot\left(\Delta t\left(L_{2}L_{1}+L_{0}\right)+\epsilon_{t}\right)\Delta t}_{\text{discretization error }}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2a" title="Theorem 2 (AdaSDE Error Decomposition). ‣ B.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs of Main Theoretical Results ‣ Adaptive Stochastic Coefficients for Accelerating Diffusion Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h3>

<div id="Thmtheorem2a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(AdaSDE Error Decomposition)<span id="Thmtheorem2a.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the same setting as Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1a" title="Theorem 1. ‣ B.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs of Main Theoretical Results ‣ Adaptive Stochastic Coefficients for Accelerating Diffusion Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. Let <math id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}_{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝖲𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}_{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the distribution after AdaSDE iteration. Then</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex62" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex62X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex62X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{1}\left(p_{t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}_{\theta}},p_{t}\right)\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝖲𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{1}\left(p_{t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}_{\theta}},p_{t}\right)\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex62X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\underbrace{B\cdot(1-\lambda(\gamma))\mathsf{TV}\left(p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}},p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\right)}_{\text{gradient error}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝖲𝖣𝖤</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">gradient error</mtext></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\underbrace{B\cdot(1-\lambda(\gamma))\mathsf{TV}\left(p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}},p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\right)}_{\text{gradient error}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex62Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex62Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\underbrace{e^{(1+\gamma)L_{2}\Delta t}(1+\gamma)\left((1+\gamma)\Delta t\left(L_{2}L_{1}+L_{0}\right)+\epsilon_{t}\right)\Delta t}_{\text{discretization error}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">discretization error</mtext></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\underbrace{e^{(1+\gamma)L_{2}\Delta t}(1+\gamma)\left((1+\gamma)\Delta t\left(L_{2}L_{1}+L_{0}\right)+\epsilon_{t}\right)\Delta t}_{\text{discretization error}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(\gamma)=2Q\left(\dfrac{B}{2\sqrt{(t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t)^{2}-t^{2}}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(\gamma)=2Q\left(\dfrac{B}{2\sqrt{(t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t)^{2}-t^{2}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\sim p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\sim p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\sim p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝖲𝖣𝖤</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\sim p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}}</annotation></semantics></math>. denote exact and generated distributions respectively. And <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\sim p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}^{\mathrm{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\sim p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}^{\mathrm{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The proof contains three key components:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ Appendix B Proofs of Main Theoretical Results ‣ Adaptive Stochastic Coefficients for Accelerating Diffusion Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, the AdaSDE process contracts the TV distance:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}-\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}-\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex63.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(1-\lambda(\gamma))\|\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}-\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(1-\lambda(\gamma))\|\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}-\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\lambda(\gamma))\|\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}-\mathbf{x}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\lambda(\gamma))\|\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}-\mathbf{x}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}\sim p^{\theta}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}\sim p^{\theta}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}\sim p_{t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}_{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝖲𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}\sim p_{t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}_{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{TV}\left(\bar{p}_{t},p_{t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}_{\theta}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝖲𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{TV}\left(\bar{p}_{t},p_{t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}_{\theta}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex65.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(1-\lambda(\gamma))\mathsf{TV}\left(\bar{p}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t},\hat{p}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(1-\lambda(\gamma))\mathsf{TV}\left(\bar{p}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t},\hat{p}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\lambda(\gamma))\mathsf{TV}\left(\bar{p}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t},p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\lambda(\gamma))\mathsf{TV}\left(\bar{p}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t},p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using the bounded trajectory assumption <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{x}\|\leq B/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{x}\|\leq B/2</annotation></semantics></math>, we convert TV to Wasserstein-1:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}\left(\bar{p}_{t},p_{t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}_{\theta}}\right)\leq B\cdot\mathsf{TV}\left(\bar{p}_{t},p_{t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}_{\theta}}\right)\leq B(1-\lambda(\gamma))\mathsf{TV}\left(\bar{p}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t},p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝖲𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝖲𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}\left(\bar{p}_{t},p_{t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}_{\theta}}\right)\leq B\cdot\mathsf{TV}\left(\bar{p}_{t},p_{t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}_{\theta}}\right)\leq B(1-\lambda(\gamma))\mathsf{TV}\left(\bar{p}_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t},p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">From Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ Appendix B Proofs of Main Theoretical Results ‣ Adaptive Stochastic Coefficients for Accelerating Diffusion Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, the local ODE error satisfies:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\gamma}-\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{\gamma}\|\leq e^{(1+\gamma)L_{2}\Delta t}(1+\gamma)\left[(1+\gamma)\Delta t(L_{2}L_{1}+L_{0})+\epsilon_{t}\right]\Delta t" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\gamma}-\bar{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{\gamma}\|\leq e^{(1+\gamma)L_{2}\Delta t}(1+\gamma)\left[(1+\gamma)\Delta t(L_{2}L_{1}+L_{0})+\epsilon_{t}\right]\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">According to Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma5" title="Lemma 5 (Connection of Wasserstein-1 distance and Norm). ‣ Appendix B Proofs of Main Theoretical Results ‣ Adaptive Stochastic Coefficients for Accelerating Diffusion Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> and Apply triangle inequality to Wasserstein distances:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{1}\left(p_{t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}_{\theta}},p_{t}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝖲𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{1}\left(p_{t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}_{\theta}},p_{t}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex69.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq W_{1}\left(\bar{p}_{t},p_{t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE_{\theta}}}\right)+W_{1}\left(\bar{p}_{t},p_{t}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝖲𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq W_{1}\left(\bar{p}_{t},p_{t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE_{\theta}}}\right)+W_{1}\left(\bar{p}_{t},p_{t}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq B(1-\lambda(\gamma))\mathsf{TV}\left(p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}},p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝖲𝖣𝖤</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq B(1-\lambda(\gamma))\mathsf{TV}\left(p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}},p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+e^{(1+\gamma)L_{2}\Delta t}(1+\gamma)\left[(1+\gamma)\Delta t(L_{2}L_{1}+L_{0})+\epsilon_{t}\right]\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+e^{(1+\gamma)L_{2}\Delta t}(1+\gamma)\left[(1+\gamma)\Delta t(L_{2}L_{1}+L_{0})+\epsilon_{t}\right]\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the error decomposition. ∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3a" title="Theorem 3 (TV comparison: AdaSDE vs. ODE). ‣ B.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs of Main Theoretical Results ‣ Adaptive Stochastic Coefficients for Accelerating Diffusion Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></h3>

<div id="Thmtheorem3a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(TV comparison: AdaSDE vs. ODE)<span id="Thmtheorem3a.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume the same conditions as in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1a" title="Theorem 1. ‣ B.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs of Main Theoretical Results ‣ Adaptive Stochastic Coefficients for Accelerating Diffusion Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2a" title="Theorem 2 (AdaSDE Error Decomposition). ‣ B.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs of Main Theoretical Results ‣ Adaptive Stochastic Coefficients for Accelerating Diffusion Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>,
and in particular that there exists a compact <math id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="diam(K)\leq B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">diam(K)\leq B</annotation></semantics></math> such that the relevant one-step distributions are supported in <math id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex72" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex72X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex72X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{\emph{(i) ODE gradient:}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext><em class="ltx_emph">(i) ODE gradient:</em></mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{\emph{(i) ODE gradient:}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex72X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}^{\mathsf{ODE}}_{\mathsf{grad}}:=B\cdot\mathsf{TV}\!\Bigl(p_{t+\Delta t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},\,p_{t+\Delta t}\Bigr)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝗀𝗋𝖺𝖽</mi><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.330em;" width="1.330em"><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}^{\mathsf{ODE}}_{\mathsf{grad}}:=B\cdot\mathsf{TV}\!\Bigl(p_{t+\Delta t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},\,p_{t+\Delta t}\Bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex72Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex72Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{\emph{(ii) AdaSDE gradient:}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext><em class="ltx_emph">(ii) AdaSDE gradient:</em></mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{\emph{(ii) AdaSDE gradient:}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex72Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}}_{\mathsf{grad}}:=B\,\bigl(1-\lambda(\gamma)\bigr)\,\mathsf{TV}\!\Bigl(p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}},\,p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\Bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝗀𝗋𝖺𝖽</mi><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝖲𝖣𝖤</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:1.330em;" width="1.330em"><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝖲𝖣𝖤</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}}_{\mathsf{grad}}:=B\,\bigl(1-\lambda(\gamma)\bigr)\,\mathsf{TV}\!\Bigl(p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}},\,p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\Bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem3a.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3a.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3a.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem3a.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(\gamma)=2\,Q\!\Bigl(\dfrac{B}{2\,\sqrt{(t+(1+\gamma)\,\Delta t)^{2}-t^{2}}}\Bigr)\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>Q</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(\gamma)=2\,Q\!\Bigl(\dfrac{B}{2\,\sqrt{(t+(1+\gamma)\,\Delta t)^{2}-t^{2}}}\Bigr)\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem3a.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is the diameter bound.
Then</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}}_{\mathsf{grad}}\;\leq\;\mathcal{E}^{\mathsf{ODE}}_{\mathsf{grad}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝗀𝗋𝖺𝖽</mi><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝖲𝖣𝖤</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝗀𝗋𝖺𝖽</mi><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}}_{\mathsf{grad}}\;\leq\;\mathcal{E}^{\mathsf{ODE}}_{\mathsf{grad}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1a" title="Theorem 1. ‣ B.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs of Main Theoretical Results ‣ Adaptive Stochastic Coefficients for Accelerating Diffusion Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\mathsf{ODE}}_{\mathsf{grad}}=B\cdot\mathsf{TV}\!\Bigl(p_{t+\Delta t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},\,p_{t+\Delta t}\Bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝗀𝗋𝖺𝖽</mi><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.330em;" width="1.330em"><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\mathsf{ODE}}_{\mathsf{grad}}=B\cdot\mathsf{TV}\!\Bigl(p_{t+\Delta t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},\,p_{t+\Delta t}\Bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">By Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2a" title="Theorem 2 (AdaSDE Error Decomposition). ‣ B.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs of Main Theoretical Results ‣ Adaptive Stochastic Coefficients for Accelerating Diffusion Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}}_{\mathsf{grad}}=B\,\bigl(1-\lambda(\gamma)\bigr)\,\mathsf{TV}\!\Bigl(p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}},\,p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\Bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝗀𝗋𝖺𝖽</mi><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝖲𝖣𝖤</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:1.330em;" width="1.330em"><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝖲𝖣𝖤</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}}_{\mathsf{grad}}=B\,\bigl(1-\lambda(\gamma)\bigr)\,\mathsf{TV}\!\Bigl(p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}},\,p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\Bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">From <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math>, AdaSDE injects Gaussian noise (a common Markov kernel) into both branches.
By Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma6" title="Lemma 6. ‣ Appendix B Proofs of Main Theoretical Results ‣ Adaptive Stochastic Coefficients for Accelerating Diffusion Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> (convolution/pushforward is nonexpansive in TV),</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}\!\Bigl(p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}},\,p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\Bigr)\;\leq\;\mathsf{TV}\!\Bigl(p_{t+\Delta t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},\,p_{t+\Delta t}\Bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.330em;" width="1.330em"><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝖲𝖣𝖤</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.330em;" width="1.330em"><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}\!\Bigl(p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}},\,p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\Bigr)\;\leq\;\mathsf{TV}\!\Bigl(p_{t+\Delta t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},\,p_{t+\Delta t}\Bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;(1-\lambda(\gamma))&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;(1-\lambda(\gamma))&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}}_{\mathsf{grad}}=B\,\bigl(1-\lambda(\gamma)\bigr)\,\mathsf{TV}\!\Bigl(p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}},\,p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\Bigr)\;\leq\;B\cdot\mathsf{TV}\!\Bigl(p_{t+\Delta t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},\,p_{t+\Delta t}\Bigr)=\mathcal{E}^{\mathsf{ODE}}_{\mathsf{grad}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝗀𝗋𝖺𝖽</mi><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝖲𝖣𝖤</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:1.330em;" width="1.330em"><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝖲𝖣𝖤</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.330em;" width="1.330em"><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝗀𝗋𝖺𝖽</mi><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}}_{\mathsf{grad}}=B\,\bigl(1-\lambda(\gamma)\bigr)\,\mathsf{TV}\!\Bigl(p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}},\,p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\Bigr)\;\leq\;B\cdot\mathsf{TV}\!\Bigl(p_{t+\Delta t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},\,p_{t+\Delta t}\Bigr)=\mathcal{E}^{\mathsf{ODE}}_{\mathsf{grad}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 2</span></span><span id="Thmremark2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(When the inequality is strict)<span id="Thmremark2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the Gaussian kernel is nondegenerate, and
<math id="Thmremark2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}\!\bigl(p_{t+\Delta t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},\,p_{t+\Delta t}\bigr)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.330em;" width="1.330em"><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}\!\bigl(p_{t+\Delta t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},\,p_{t+\Delta t}\bigr)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>
(equivalently, the two pre-smoothing distributions are not a.e. equal and admit <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> densities), then</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}\!\Bigl(p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}},\,p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\Bigr)\;&lt;\;\mathsf{TV}\!\Bigl(p_{t+\Delta t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},\,p_{t+\Delta t}\Bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.330em;" width="1.330em"><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝖲𝖣𝖤</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">&lt;</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.330em;" width="1.330em"><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}\!\Bigl(p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}},\,p_{t+(1+\gamma)\Delta t}\Bigr)\;&lt;\;\mathsf{TV}\!\Bigl(p_{t+\Delta t}^{\mathsf{ODE}_{\theta}},\,p_{t+\Delta t}\Bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmremark2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and hence <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}}_{\mathsf{grad}}&lt;\mathcal{E}^{\mathsf{ODE}}_{\mathsf{grad}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝗀𝗋𝖺𝖽</mi><mi>𝖠𝖽𝖺𝖲𝖣𝖤</mi></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝗀𝗋𝖺𝖽</mi><mi>𝖮𝖣𝖤</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\mathsf{AdaSDE}}_{\mathsf{grad}}&lt;\mathcal{E}^{\mathsf{ODE}}_{\mathsf{grad}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>More on AdaSDE</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Experiment details.</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Experiment detail in main result</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Since AdaSDE has fewer than 40 parameters, its training incurs minimal computational cost. We train <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> for 10K images, which only takes 5-10 minutes on CIFAR10 with a single 4090 GPU and about 20 minutes on LSUN Bedroom with four 4090 GPUs. For generating reference teacher trajectories, we use DPM-Solver-2 with M=3. For tuning across all datasets, we employed a learning rate of 0.2 along with a cosine learning rate schedule (coslr). The random seed was fixed to 0 to ensure consistent reproducibility of the experimental results. To ensure the robustness of our experimental results, we conducted ten independent runs for each NFE (Number of Function Evaluations) setting on the CIFAR10 dataset. Across these runs, the FID (Fréchet Inception Distance) scores consistently varied by no more than 0.1.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Time uniform scheme</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite> proposes a discretization scheme for diffusion sampling given the starting <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, end time <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote the number of steps as <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, then the <span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">time uniform</span> discretization scheme is:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex79.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(e^{0.5\,\beta_{d}\,t^{2}+\beta_{\min}\,t}-1\right)^{0.5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>0.5</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(e^{0.5\,\beta_{d}\,t^{2}+\beta_{\min}\,t}-1\right)^{0.5}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex80"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma^{-1}(\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma^{-1}(\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex80.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{\beta_{\min}^{2}+2\,\beta_{d}\,\ln\!\left(\sigma^{2}+1\right)}-\beta_{\min}}{\beta_{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{\beta_{\min}^{2}+2\,\beta_{d}\,\ln\!\left(\sigma^{2}+1\right)}-\beta_{\min}}{\beta_{d}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta_{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex81.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{2\left(\ln\!\left(\sigma_{\min}^{2}+1\right)/\epsilon_{s}-\ln\!\left(\sigma_{\max}^{2}+1\right)\right)}{\epsilon_{s}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{2\left(\ln\!\left(\sigma_{\min}^{2}+1\right)/\epsilon_{s}-\ln\!\left(\sigma_{\max}^{2}+1\right)\right)}{\epsilon_{s}-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex82.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\ln\!\left(\sigma_{\max}^{2}+1\right)-0.5\,\beta_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\ln\!\left(\sigma_{\max}^{2}+1\right)-0.5\,\beta_{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle t_{\text{temp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>temp</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle t_{\text{temp}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex83.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(1+\frac{i}{N-1}\left(\epsilon_{s}^{1/\rho}-1\right)\right)^{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>ρ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(1+\frac{i}{N-1}\left(\epsilon_{s}^{1/\rho}-1\right)\right)^{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex84.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma\!\left(t_{\text{temp}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.437em;" width="0.437em"><mi>σ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>temp</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma\!\left(t_{\text{temp}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We set <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\max}=80.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>80.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\max}=80.0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\min}=0.002" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.002</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\min}=0.002</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{s}=10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{s}=10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math> across all datasets in our experiments.</p>
</div>
</section>
